<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark">
  <title>${project_name} Readme</title>
  <meta name="description" content="${project_name_short} (${display_name}): an open-source engine for the Quake Live you already own. Installation, features and documentation.">
  <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="${icon_data_uri}">
  <style>
    :root {
      --bg: #08080a;
      --bg-2: #0e0e11;
      --panel: #131317;
      --panel-2: #1a1a1f;
      --line: #2a2a31;
      --line-strong: #3a3a43;
      --text: #ececf0;
      --muted: #a6a6b0;
      --steel: #c9cdd3;
      --red: #d0141b;
      --red-bright: #ff3b30;
      --red-deep: #8a0a10;
      --font-head: "Montserrat", "Segoe UI Black", "Segoe UI", "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
      --font-body: "Segoe UI", system-ui, -apple-system, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
      --font-label: "Bahnschrift", "DIN Alternate", "Segoe UI", Arial, sans-serif;
      --font-mono: "Cascadia Mono", "Cascadia Code", Consolas, "DejaVu Sans Mono", monospace;
      --carbon:
        repeating-linear-gradient(45deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.018) 0 2px, transparent 2px 6px),
        repeating-linear-gradient(-45deg, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35) 0 2px, transparent 2px 6px);
    }

    * { box-sizing: border-box; }

    html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      background: var(--carbon), radial-gradient(ellipse at 50% -10%, #2a0b0d 0%, var(--bg) 55%) fixed, var(--bg);
      color: var(--text);
      font: 16px/1.65 var(--font-body);
      -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
    }

    a { color: var(--red-bright); text-underline-offset: 3px; }
    a:hover { color: #fff; }
    a:focus-visible, .button:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--red-bright); outline-offset: 3px; }

    code {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.9em;
      padding: 0.12em 0.42em;
      border-radius: 5px;
      background: #1d1d23;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      color: #f1f1f4;
      overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }

    .wrap { width: min(1080px, calc(100% - 32px)); margin: 0 auto; }

    /* ---------- hero ---------- */
    .hero {
      position: relative;
      overflow: hidden;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
      background: var(--carbon), linear-gradient(180deg, #111114 0%, #08080a 100%);
    }

    .hero::before,
    .hero::after {
      content: "";
      position: absolute;
      top: -10%;
      bottom: -10%;
      width: 34px;
      background: var(--red);
      transform: skewX(-18deg);
      pointer-events: none;
    }

    .hero::before { right: 9%; box-shadow: 70px 0 0 -6px rgba(208, 20, 27, 0.55), 132px 0 0 -12px rgba(208, 20, 27, 0.3); }
    .hero::after { left: -30px; width: 14px; opacity: 0.8; }

    .hero-inner {
      position: relative;
      z-index: 1;
      padding: 48px 0 40px;
    }

    .eyebrow {
      margin: 0 0 18px;
      font: 600 0.78rem/1 var(--font-label);
      letter-spacing: 0.32em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--muted);
    }

    .eyebrow::before { content: "// "; color: var(--red-bright); letter-spacing: 0; }

    .logo {
      display: block;
      width: min(520px, 100%);
      height: auto;
      filter: drop-shadow(0 18px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55));
    }

    h1 {
      margin: 26px 0 0;
      font: italic 900 clamp(1.9rem, 4.6vw, 3.2rem)/1.05 var(--font-head);
      letter-spacing: 0.005em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    h1 span { display: block; color: var(--red-bright); }

    .subtitle {
      max-width: 720px;
      margin: 18px 0 0;
      color: #d4d4da;
      font-size: 1.08rem;
    }

    .buttons { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; margin-top: 26px; }

    .button {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      padding: 11px 20px;
      border-radius: 6px;
      border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
      background: rgba(20, 20, 24, 0.85);
      color: var(--text);
      text-decoration: none;
      font: 600 0.82rem/1 var(--font-label);
      letter-spacing: 0.14em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      transition: border-color 120ms ease, background 120ms ease, transform 120ms ease;
    }

    .button:hover { border-color: var(--red-bright); color: #fff; transform: translateY(-1px); }

    .button-primary {
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--red-bright) 0%, var(--red) 55%, var(--red-deep) 100%);
      border-color: var(--red);
      color: #fff;
      box-shadow: 0 10px 26px rgba(208, 20, 27, 0.32);
    }

    .facts {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(210px, 1fr));
      gap: 1px;
      margin-top: 34px;
      background: var(--line);
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 10px;
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    .fact { padding: 14px 18px; background: rgba(14, 14, 17, 0.92); }

    .fact strong {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 4px;
      font: 600 0.72rem/1.2 var(--font-label);
      letter-spacing: 0.2em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--muted);
    }

    .fact span { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }

    /* ---------- navigation ---------- */
    nav {
      position: sticky;
      top: 0;
      z-index: 5;
      background: rgba(8, 8, 10, 0.92);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
      backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
    }

    nav .wrap { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px 24px; padding: 11px 0; }

    nav a {
      color: var(--muted);
      text-decoration: none;
      font: 600 0.74rem/1.4 var(--font-label);
      letter-spacing: 0.18em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    nav a:hover { color: #fff; }

    /* ---------- sections ---------- */
    main { padding: 8px 0 24px; }

    section { padding: 46px 0 6px; scroll-margin-top: 48px; }

    h2 {
      margin: 0 0 6px;
      font: italic 900 clamp(1.35rem, 2.6vw, 1.75rem)/1.15 var(--font-head);
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    }

    h2 .num { color: var(--red-bright); margin-right: 0.35em; }

    .rule {
      height: 4px;
      width: 76px;
      margin: 10px 0 20px;
      background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--red) 0 60%, transparent 60% 70%, var(--red-deep) 70% 100%);
      transform: skewX(-18deg);
    }

    h3 {
      margin: 0 0 8px;
      font: 700 1.02rem/1.3 var(--font-body);
      color: #fff;
    }

    .lead { max-width: 820px; margin: 0 0 14px; color: #d4d4da; }

    p { margin: 0 0 12px; }

    .note { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.95rem; }

    .points { margin: 0 0 16px; padding: 0; list-style: none; }

    .points li { position: relative; padding-left: 22px; margin: 8px 0; }

    .points li::before {
      content: "";
      position: absolute;
      left: 2px;
      top: 0.62em;
      width: 9px;
      height: 9px;
      background: var(--red);
      transform: skewX(-18deg);
    }

    .grid { display: grid; gap: 14px; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 300px), 1fr)); }

    .card {
      position: relative;
      padding: 18px 20px;
      background: var(--panel);
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 10px;
      transition: border-color 120ms ease;
    }

    .card::before {
      content: "";
      position: absolute;
      left: 20px;
      top: -1px;
      width: 38px;
      height: 3px;
      background: var(--red);
    }

    .card:hover { border-color: var(--line-strong); }

    .card p, .card li { color: #c9c9d1; font-size: 0.96rem; }

    .card ol { margin: 6px 0 0; padding-left: 20px; }

    .card ol li { margin: 6px 0; }

    .steps { counter-reset: step; list-style: none; margin: 4px 0 0; padding: 0; }

    .steps li { counter-increment: step; position: relative; padding-left: 40px; margin: 12px 0; }

    .steps li::before {
      content: counter(step);
      position: absolute;
      left: 0;
      top: 0;
      width: 26px;
      height: 26px;
      display: grid;
      place-items: center;
      background: var(--red);
      color: #fff;
      font: italic 800 0.86rem/1 var(--font-head);
      transform: skewX(-12deg);
      border-radius: 3px;
    }

    table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 6px 0 16px; font-size: 0.95rem; }

    th, td { padding: 9px 12px; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }

    th {
      font: 600 0.72rem/1.3 var(--font-label);
      letter-spacing: 0.18em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--muted);
    }

    .table-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }

    .docs a { font-weight: 600; }

    .tag {
      display: inline-block;
      margin-left: 6px;
      padding: 1px 7px;
      border-radius: 4px;
      background: rgba(208, 20, 27, 0.16);
      color: #ff8a84;
      font: 600 0.66rem/1.6 var(--font-label);
      letter-spacing: 0.14em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      vertical-align: 2px;
    }

    footer {
      margin-top: 40px;
      padding: 26px 0 40px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.88rem;
    }

    footer p { max-width: 860px; }

    @media (max-width: 640px) {
      .hero::before { right: -40px; opacity: 0.6; }
      .hero-inner { padding: 32px 0 28px; }
      .button { flex: 1 1 100%; justify-content: center; }
      section { padding-top: 34px; }
    }

    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      html { scroll-behavior: auto; }
      .button, .card { transition: none; }
      .button:hover { transform: none; }
    }

    @media print {
      body { background: #fff; color: #111; }
      .hero, .fact, .card { background: #fff; }
      .hero::before, .hero::after, nav, .buttons { display: none; }
      h1, h2, h3, .fact span, .lead, .card p, .card li { color: #111; }
      a { color: #8a0a10; }
      code { background: #f3f3f3; color: #111; border-color: #ddd; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">${display_name} · Readme</p>
      ${logo_svg}
      <h1>The Quake Live you own. <span>Rebuilt engine.</span></h1>
      <p class="subtitle"><strong>${project_name_short}</strong> is an open-source engine for the retail Steam release of Quake Live. It keeps the game you know, then adds faster rendering, modern audio and input, stronger platform support and a long list of quality-of-life improvements.</p>
      <div class="buttons">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/releases/latest">Latest release</a>
        <a class="button" href="#getting-started">Getting started</a>
        <a class="button" href="#documentation">Documentation</a>
        <a class="button" href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/blob/main/BUILD.md">Build guide</a>
        <a class="button" href="LICENSE">License</a>
      </div>
      <div class="facts">
        <div class="fact"><strong>Compatibility target</strong><span>${compatibility_target}</span></div>
        <div class="fact"><strong>Version line</strong><span>${base_version}</span></div>
        <div class="fact"><strong>Official packages</strong><span>Windows x86 client · Linux i686 server</span></div>
        <div class="fact"><strong>Requires</strong><span>Quake Live on Steam (app 282440)</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <nav aria-label="Sections">
    <div class="wrap">
      <a href="#introduction">Introduction</a>
      <a href="#features">Features</a>
      <a href="#getting-started">Getting started</a>
      <a href="#documentation">Documentation</a>
      <a href="#credits">Credits</a>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <main class="wrap">
    <section id="introduction">
      <h2><span class="num">1.</span>Introduction</h2>
      <div class="rule"></div>
      <p class="lead">Retail Quake Live compatibility comes first:</p>
      <ul class="points">
        <li><strong>FnQL players join retail servers</strong>, and <strong>retail players join FnQL servers</strong> and receive exactly what a retail server would send them.</li>
        <li>Your install, profile, configs, <code>.dm_91</code> demos, maps and Workshop content keep working.</li>
        <li>Steam authentication goes through Steam's own session tickets and is never faked.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>FnQL is engine-only. It does not reconstruct or distribute Quake Live game code or assets, so a legitimate <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/282440/Quake_Live/">Quake Live installation on Steam</a> is required. Its lineage runs from id Software's GPL Quake III Arena source through ioquake3, Quake3e and FnQ3.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="features">
      <h2><span class="num">2.</span>Features</h2>
      <div class="rule"></div>
      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Extensive Quake Live compatibility</h3>
          <p>Built around the retail Steam release, with support for official assets and game modules, protocol 91 networking, <code>.dm_91</code> demos, BSP v47 maps, advertisements, factories, player profiles, the retail WebUI, Steam integration and Workshop content.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Fast, modern hardware rendering</h3>
          <p>Choose between optimized <strong>GLx</strong> and <strong>Vulkan</strong> renderers, plus an experimental <strong>Vulkan RTX</strong> module, with GPU-cached world geometry, optimized lightmaps, reduced rendering overhead, improved depth precision and better performance on large or demanding maps.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Modern visual upgrades</h3>
          <p>Optional HDR rendering and output, MSAA, supersampling, render scaling, anisotropic filtering, bloom, tone mapping, colour grading, shadow-mapped dynamic lights, sun shadows from each map's own sky, motion blur, lens flares, soft particles, enhanced liquids and per-map fog.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Improved player visibility</h3>
          <p>Optional player rim lighting, stencil outlines or both, with configurable enemy, teammate, team and free-for-all colours, intensity and outline thickness. Cel shading, model outlines and world-edge outlines are also available.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Better modern hardware and OS support</h3>
          <p>Native Win32 and X11 video and input in release builds (SDL3 for source builds), OpenAL audio, modern graphics APIs, high-resolution and high-refresh displays, borderless/windowed/fullscreen modes, fast Alt+Enter switching and improved compatibility with current desktop systems.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Low-latency, configurable controls</h3>
          <p>Raw mouse input, Quake Live-accurate CPI scaling, signed acceleration, sensitivity caps and angle-history filtering, while retaining classic Quake3e/ioquake3 mouse styles. Controllers, including Quake Live's analog gamepad mapping on Windows, and Unicode text input are also supported (enable controllers with <code>in_joystick 1</code>; SDL builds add controller hotplugging).</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Modern spatial audio</h3>
          <p>OpenAL and HRTF headphone positioning, surround output, reverb, geometry-based occlusion, output-device selection, live device recovery and automatic fallback to the classic software mixer.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Major quality-of-life improvements</h3>
          <p>Scalable TTF console text, smooth scrolling, mouse selection, clipboard support, drag-and-drop editing, live command/CVar/map completion, minimize hotkeys, focus muting, lower background CPU usage and more flexible player configuration.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Better screenshots, video and streaming tools</h3>
          <p>PNG, TGA, JPEG and BMP capture, clipboard screenshots, custom filenames, camera metadata, configurable levelshots, watermarks, cubemap capture, arbitrary-resolution output, FFmpeg video piping and a windowless capture client.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Faster content handling</h3>
          <p>Quicker startup and map restarts with large PK3 libraries, raised filesystem and map limits, fast redirected downloads and automatic handling of server-required Workshop content.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Greater stability and security</h3>
          <p>Extensive Quake3e and FnQ3 bug fixes, improved memory management, lower memory usage, stronger network protection, hostile-content checks on downloaded packages and graceful fallbacks when optional rendering, audio, WebUI or Steam functionality is unavailable.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="getting-started">
      <h2><span class="num">3.</span>Getting Started</h2>
      <div class="rule"></div>
      <p class="lead">Install <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/282440/Quake_Live/">Quake Live through Steam</a> and launch the retail game once, so Steam creates its normal files and your player profile. Then add the FnQL package for your platform.</p>
      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Windows client</h3>
          <ol class="steps">
            <li>In Steam, right-click Quake Live → <strong>Manage</strong> → <strong>Browse local files</strong>, and extract the Windows <code>.zip</code> into that folder.</li>
            <li>Keep <code>FnQL-pkg.fnz</code>, <code>fnql-web.pak</code>, the renderer modules and the packaged runtime libraries beside <code>fnql.exe</code>.</li>
            <li>Leave Steam running and launch <code>fnql.exe</code>.</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="note">FnQL's files sit beside the retail ones; <code>quakelive_steam.exe</code> keeps working as before. The official build is Win32/x86 so it can load the retail game modules and WebUI.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Linux dedicated server</h3>
          <ol class="steps">
            <li>Install the 32-bit runtime libraries reported by <code>ldd ./fnql.ded</code>. The release is i686 so it can load retail <code>qagamei386.so</code> from <code>baseq3/bin.pk3</code>.</li>
            <li>Extract with <code>tar -xzf fnql-*-linux-x86.tar.gz -C "&lt;Quake Live folder&gt;"</code> to keep the executable bits.</li>
            <li>From that folder run <code>./fnql.ded +set fs_steampath "$$PWD" +set dedicated 2 +map campgrounds ffa</code>.</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="note">Keep the two FnQL package sidecars and renderer modules beside the binaries.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="note">FnQL discovers conventional Steam libraries on each supported OS; for a custom library use <code>+set fs_steampath "&lt;Quake Live folder&gt;"</code>. Optional Steam and WebUI services fail safely when unavailable.</p>

      <h3 style="margin-top: 26px;">Game modules</h3>
      <p>Every package puts the clean-room <a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL-game">FnQL-game</a> modules in <code>baseq3/</code>, and FnQL uses them by default. Retail clients join FnQL servers running the FnQL-game game module and see what a retail server would send them.</p>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Cvar</th><th>Values</th><th>What it picks</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>vm_gameProvider</code></td><td><code>auto</code> (default), <code>fnql</code>, <code>retail</code></td><td>Server game module</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>vm_cgameProvider</code></td><td><code>auto</code> (default), <code>fnql</code>, <code>retail</code></td><td>Client game module</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>vm_uiProvider</code></td><td><code>auto</code> (default), <code>fnql</code>, <code>retail</code></td><td>Menu module</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="note"><code>auto</code> takes an FnQL-game module that declares retail wire parity, as the bundled ones do, and falls back to the retail module when it is missing; <code>vminfo</code> shows which module is active. A configuration written by an earlier FnQL release holds <code>vm_gameProvider "retail"</code>, its old default; FnQL moves it to the new default once, so set the provider again afterwards to keep the retail module. On pure servers, FnQL-game's cgame and UI run only from <code>baseq3/fnql_game_client.pk3</code> when the server lists it in <code>sv_fnqlClientPaks</code>; elsewhere, retail servers included, FnQL loads the retail cgame and UI.</p>

      <h3 style="margin-top: 26px;">What's in this package</h3>
      <ul class="points">
        <li>The Windows package contains FnQL's open-source engine, its WebUI overlay, the FnQL-game modules and the compiled, closed-source Steam provider (<code>fnql_steam.dll</code>), which talks to the <code>steam_api.dll</code> from your own install. The Linux package contains only redistributable FnQL components and the FnQL-game modules.</li>
        <li>No package includes Valve's <code>steam_api.dll</code> or any retail game content.</li>
        <li>The FnQL-game modules combine FnQL-game's own code (GPLv2 or later) with baseq3a baseline code under id Software's Quake III Arena game-source license: see <code>docs/fnql/FNQL_GAME_BINARY_NOTICE.txt</code> and <code>docs/fnql-game/</code>.</li>
        <li>Releases ship only the x86 packages. FnQL also builds from source for x86_64 on Windows and Linux, and its dedicated server for Linux aarch64, armv7l, ppc64le and ppc64; those builds have no Steam integration, WebUI or retail modules yet and run the FnQL-game modules. There is no macOS build, because retail ships no macOS game, client, UI or QVM modules.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="documentation" class="docs">
      <h2><span class="num">4.</span>Documentation</h2>
      <div class="rule"></div>
      <p class="lead">Guides marked <span class="tag">included</span> ship in this package; the rest open on GitHub.</p>
      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Player guides</h3>
          <ul class="points">
            <li><a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/blob/main/docs/DISPLAY.md">Display Guide</a>: renderers, display modes, HDR, scaling, anti-aliasing, bloom, lighting, shadows, fog, liquids, lens flares and motion blur.</li>
            <li><a href="docs/RTX.md">RTX Renderer Guide</a><span class="tag">included</span>: requirements, selection, fallback, safe settings and troubleshooting.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/blob/main/docs/VISUALS.md">Visuals Guide</a>: player highlighting, colours, cel shading and outlines.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/blob/main/docs/ASPECT_CORRECTION.md">Aspect Handling Guide</a>: the retail WebUI, menus and cinematics.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/blob/main/docs/AUDIO.md">Audio Guide</a>: devices, HRTF, spatial effects, fallback and troubleshooting.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/blob/main/docs/CONSOLE.md">Console Guide</a>: layout, scaling, completion, clipboard and mouse use.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/blob/main/docs/SCREENSHOTS.md">Screenshot Guide</a>: formats, filenames, metadata, levelshots, watermarks and cubemaps.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/releases">Release History</a>: changelogs and downloads.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Technical and build docs</h3>
          <ul class="points">
            <li><a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/blob/main/BUILD.md">Build Guide</a>: compiling FnQL locally.</li>
            <li><a href="docs/GLX.md">GLx Renderer Guide</a><span class="tag">included</span>: the default OpenGL-lineage renderer, diagnostics and troubleshooting.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/blob/main/docs/fnql/INPUT_COMPATIBILITY.md">Input Compatibility Notes</a>: retail mouse math, text input, controllers and legacy profiles.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/blob/main/docs/fnql/WEBUI_BACKEND.md">WebUI Backend Notes</a>: retail resources, platform boundaries, overlay order and fallbacks.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/blob/main/docs/fnql/STEAM_PROVIDER.md">Steam Provider Notes</a>: the open loader ABI, provider distribution and runtime policy.</li>
            <li><a href="docs/fnql/RTX_RENDERER.md">RTX Renderer Contract</a><span class="tag">included</span>: the Quake Live ABI boundary, conservative defaults and runtime validation.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/blob/main/docs/fnql/GAME_MODULES.md">Game Modules</a>: module providers and how FnQL hosts FnQL-game without breaking retail interoperability.</li>
            <li><a href="docs/fnql/TECHNICAL.md">Technical Notes</a><span class="tag">included</span>: repository structure, release flow, compatibility workflow and maintainer conventions.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="credits">
      <h2><span class="num">5.</span>Credits</h2>
      <div class="rule"></div>
      <p class="lead">FnQL follows a clear upstream lineage from the <a href="https://github.com/id-Software/Quake-III-Arena">Quake III Arena SDK</a>, through <a href="https://github.com/ioquake3/ioq3">ioquake3</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ec-/Quake3e">Quake3e</a>, <a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQ3">FnQ3</a> and <a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/QL-SRP">QL-SRP</a>.</p>
      <p>Additional compatibility and feature work draws from projects and references such as <a href="https://bitbucket.org/CPMADevs/cnq3">CNQ3</a>, <a href="https://github.com/zturtleman/spearmint">Spearmint</a>, <a href="https://github.com/brugal/wolfcamql">WolfcamQL</a>, Luigi Auriemma's <a href="https://aluigi.altervista.org/papers.htm#qldec">qldec</a> and <a href="https://github.com/Paril/DarkMatter-Q2">DarkMatter-Q2</a>. See the full chain and acknowledgements in <a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/blob/main/CREDITS.md">CREDITS.md</a>.</p>
